{
  "gate": "arc-a770-pack-persist-20261125",
  "title": "Bonsai 2.5 27B ternary shapes on the Arc A770: persistent eight-row work list against the per-shape GEMV",
  "measured": "2026-11-25",
  "commit": "unreleased",
  "command": "python -m kindi intel-pack --pack pack --device-name Arc --repeats 20 --json run-{25mtp,bonsai2}-persist-<n>.json",
  "notes": "The same pack bytes read twice: the per-shape four-row phase-split GEMV with a reduce launch per matrix, and the persistent kernel that gives each work-item eight rows and covers every ternary tensor in one work list at parts=1 (no reduce). Both are weight-streaming projections, not model runs: attention, norms, GDN, the f32 head and the KV cache are excluded. Three spaced runs per pack, twenty timed launches per chunk, host idle. The five-launch runs of the same command measured 168-233 GB/s, so twenty repeats is what this gate quotes.",
  "evidence": [
    "docs/benchmarks/2026-11-25-i7-8086k-arc-a770-pack/run-25mtp-persist-1.json",
    "docs/benchmarks/2026-11-25-i7-8086k-arc-a770-pack/run-25mtp-persist-2.json",
    "docs/benchmarks/2026-11-25-i7-8086k-arc-a770-pack/run-25mtp-persist-3.json",
